<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  One URL, because that is honestly all there is: the app is a single page and
  every screen inside it is a state, not an address. A sitemap listing invented
  fragment URLs would not help.

  Not auto-discovered. A crawler looks for the sitemap named in robots.txt at
  the ROOT of the domain (jo0dile.github.io/robots.txt), and this is a project
  page under /MyMenuPack/, so nothing here can point at it. It has to be
  submitted by hand in Google Search Console.

  Deliberately minimal. The first version declared hreflang alternates for en,
  ar and x-default that all pointed at this same URL — which describes nothing,
  because the app switches language in the browser and has one address either
  way. Alternates exist to map one language to one URL each; three of them
  aimed at a single URL is noise in a file whose whole job is to be parsed
  without argument.

  No lastmod for the same reason: a hardcoded date would start lying the day
  after it was written, and Google discounts a lastmod it learns not to trust.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://jo0dile.github.io/MyMenuPack/</loc>
    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
    <priority>1.0</priority>
  </url>
</urlset>
